PUBLISHING
----------
The website is a static HTML site and can be hosted on Cloudflare Pages,
GitHub Pages, Netlify, or another static hosting service.

Cloudflare Pages setup:
1. Create a GitHub repository.
2. Upload index.html to the repository root.
3. Upload the entire assets folder.
4. Connect the repository to Cloudflare Pages.
5. Deploy the site.
6. Use the generated Pages URL or connect a custom domain.

IMPORTANT
---------
Keep index.html and the assets folder together. Image paths in the HTML depend
on the files remaining in the assets folder.

The portfolio images are presented as samples/illustrative work where
applicable. Do not add unsupported testimonials, statistics, credentials,
client claims, or project results.

EDITING
-------
Website text, Fiverr links, email, and other settings can be edited in
index.html.

For future portfolio updates, add the new images to the assets folder and
update the corresponding image references in index.html.

